    evidence: "NIAAA describes effective alcohol treatment as a combination of behavioral care, mutual support when desired, and medications when appropriate. FDA-approved options for alcohol use disorder include naltrexone, acamprosate, and disulfiram, and a qualified prescriber should explain expected benefits, limitations, and health considerations.",
