    safety: "Overdose risk is especially high with fentanyl exposure, mixing opioids with alcohol or benzodiazepines, or returning to use after tolerance has fallen. Patients and close contacts should know how to recognize an overdose, call 911, give naloxone, provide rescue breathing when trained, and stay until emergency help arrives.",
